Task: Phase 6 architectural fix — chore_home_network_deployment_hardening_20260712

WHY
The clean-image SPA build failed intermittently with the Vite/Rollup family
'Rollup failed to resolve import "<dep>" from "/app/app/..."', naming a
different module each run. Two prior root-cause claims (overlay write-visibility
between RUN layers; install layout / npm ci flags) were both retracted. The
defect blocked a trustworthy home-network deployment image.

MECHANISM (proven, not inferred)
rollup maxParallelFileOps default = 1000 (getMaxParallelFileOps,
rollup/dist/shared/rollup.js:23403, rollup 4.57.1)
buildah RUN layer fd soft limit  = 1024

Peak fd demand measured with ulimit raised to 65536 (so the reading is not
clipped by the limit under test):
  uncapped  -> 1029  (1000 queue slots + ~29 baseline)   5 over the limit
  cap 128   ->  156  (128 + ~28)                          6.6x headroom

The five-descriptor overshoot is the intermittency. It explains every prior
symptom simultaneously: different module per run, failures in the 118-143
module band, 13 consecutive greens, and clean runs under podman run / on host
where the limit is 1048576.

WHY THE EXCLUSION HELD SO LONG
(1) Namespace error: the fd limit had been measured under 'podman run' and on
    the host, neither of which is where a build layer executes. Verified in
    this session: buildah RUN 1024 / podman run 1048576 / host 1048576.
(2) Incomplete measurement: only the LIMIT was ever measured. The build's
    DEMAND was the missing number.

CONTROLLED REPRODUCTION (host, 40s, no container)
  ulimit -n 1024 + cap removed ->
  [commonjs--resolver] Could not load .../lucide-react/dist/esm/icons/
  line-dot-right-horizontal.js: EMFILE: too many open files
First observation of EMFILE for this defect. rollup surfaces the same
exhaustion as 'failed to resolve' depending on which open() loses, so the
error text was never the defect's identity.

